From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: q6afe: wait for the DSP audio services before probing

On SM8250 the LPASS VA macro intermittently fails to probe at boot:

  qcom-q6afe aprsvc:service:4:4: cmd = 0x100f4 returned error = 0x16
  qcom-q6afe aprsvc:service:4:4: Unknown cmd 0x100f4
  qcom-q6afe aprsvc:service:4:4: AFE failed to vote (3)
  va_macro 3370000.codec: probe with driver va_macro failed with error -110

Its first LPASS core vote (AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST,
sent by clk_prepare_enable() of the "macro" vote clock) goes out ~11 ms
after the APR services appear and the DSP rejects it. The probe error is
not -EPROBE_DEFER, so the VA macro stays unbound and the rx/tx/wsa
macros, both SoundWire buses and the sound card wait behind it for the
rest of the boot. The same firmware wins the race on other boots.

The downstream audio stack never sends that vote early: before bringing
audio up it polls AVCS_CMD_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE until the DSP reports
its audio services (AVS) up, with the comment "ADSP will be coming up
after boot up and AVS might not be fully up when the control reaches
here". Mainline has that query as q6core_is_adsp_ready(), with no
caller.

1. q6afe_probe() waits for q6core_is_adsp_ready() before it creates
   the ports and the clock controller whose prepare sends the vote,
   and defers if the DSP is not up (or q6core has not probed yet).
   Needs the previous patch, without which the check reports "ready"
   precisely when the DSP does not answer.

2. q6afe_callback() did not handle a basic response for the vote
   opcodes, so a rejected vote was logged as "Unknown cmd" and its
   waiter ran out the full 3 s timeout with the DSP's status already
   in hand. Complete the waiter with that status instead; an unvote
   has no waiter and is only logged.

The ready wait is logged once ("DSP audio services ready after N ms")
so a boot shows whether the gate engaged.

[ARMDeck: from Nova-Deck os-build, kernel/patches/0895 (commit 325dfde9a380),
unchanged except for context offsets. On the OnePlus 8 the same rejected
vote (0x100f4, error 0x16, "AFE failed to vote (3)") leaves the LPASS pin
controller (33c0000.pinctrl) at -110, so the sound card is missing on about
1 boot in 5 (docs/gaming-stack.md, TODO 16).]

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index 980851a..ec9e9ff 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -990,6 +990,20 @@ static int q6afe_callback(struct apr_device *adev, struct apr_resp_pkt *data)
 				wake_up(&afe->wait);
 			}
 			break;
+		case AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST:
+			/*
+			 * A rejected vote comes back as a basic response, not
+			 * as AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST.
+			 * Complete the waiter with the DSP's status instead
+			 * of leaving it to time out.
+			 */
+			afe->result.opcode = AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST;
+			afe->result.status = res->status;
+			wake_up(&afe->wait);
+			break;
+		case AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_DEVOTE_REQUEST:
+			/* Nobody waits for an unvote; the status is logged above. */
+			break;
 		default:
 			dev_err(afe->dev, "Unknown cmd 0x%x\n",	res->opcode);
 			break;
@@ -1900,6 +1914,20 @@ static int q6afe_probe(struct apr_device *adev)
 {
 	struct q6afe *afe;
 	struct device *dev = &adev->dev;
+	unsigned long start = jiffies;
+
+	/*
+	 * The APR services appear before the DSP's audio services are up.
+	 * A request that arrives in that window is rejected: the LPASS core
+	 * vote a codec macro sends from its probe is refused, and that
+	 * probe fails for the rest of the boot. Wait for the DSP to report
+	 * itself ready before creating the ports and clocks that talk to it.
+	 */
+	if (!q6core_is_adsp_ready())
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "DSP audio services not ready\n");
+	dev_info(dev, "DSP audio services ready after %u ms\n",
+		 jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - start));
 
 	afe = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*afe), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!afe)
